Description: Fast file manager with tabs, previews and a built-in terminal
 Prime Files is a file explorer written in Rust: tabs in the title bar, a
 split view, previews of images, video, audio, PDF, 3D models and text, an
 embedded terminal and a quick search over the disk.
 .
 It is the Linux port of the Windows program of the same name, which keeps
 its own name inside the code (the crates are still called nohrs-*).
 .
 The Windows-only parts are not there: the Explorer's context menu, the
 NTFS index in the Everything style, the Listary plugin, the Shell
 thumbnails and the in-app auto-updater.
